1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:06,424
A New Year print begins as a drawing, carved backwards into a plank of pear wood.

2
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:09,011
One block holds every line.

3
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:13,450
Then comes colour, one block at a time.

4
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:16,531
Peach for the skin. Yellow for the gold.

5
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:20,869
Then green for the lotus. Indigo for the water.

6
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:24,994
No block fits quite perfectly. That is the charm.

7
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:30,203
Red goes last. A carp for surplus. A lotus for year after year.

8
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:33,950
But a wish needs a guard.

9
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:38,638
So one block is printed twice, and the pair face each other.

10
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:43,306
Then someone opens the door.

11
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:47,059
And the old year tears.

12
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:52,173
The paper was only borrowed. The block stays on the bench.

13
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,551
Next year, it prints again.
